Notebook[{
Cell["Ancient DNA Lactase Persistence", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"b28422fc-91ff-4d3d-8369-216c36118626"],

Cell["\<\
A spatial diffusion-selection model for rs4988235 fitted with SMC-ABC, in \
Wolfram Language\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"131d57d3-8507-4791-a300-4b69963344bc"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook walks through the full pipeline interactively: data retrieval \
and parsing, regional binomial logistic reproduction, the coarse spatial \
model, SMC-ABC inference with spatial-gradient summary statistics, posterior \
predictive checks, held-out validation, sensitivity analysis, and the \
calibrated maps and animation. The reusable code lives in \
src/LactasePersistenceSpatial.wl; scripts/run_pipeline.wls runs everything \
non-interactively. Interactive settings below are slightly smaller than the \
script defaults so each step stays responsive; results in the repository \
README and the Wolfram Community post use the script defaults (400 particles, \
5 generations).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e99dfe9-4314-4a18-9838-537c992beebe"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"15818ff7-0fbd-4117-a202-403215e1f9ee"],

Cell["\<\
SetDirectory[ParentDirectory[NotebookDirectory[]]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{Directory[], \"src\", \"LactasePersistenceSpatial.wl\"}]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"a8dceada-2469-426d-817e-9f60db68f0c6"],

Cell["Data", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"f1bd07a5-e6cf-43f0-af86-88ff26b89e08"],

Cell["\<\
Download the public GLAD ancient rs4988235 workbook (derived from AADR v44.3, \
used for Evershed et al. 2022) if it is not already present, parse it, and \
keep the samples with a genotype call, an age, and coordinates. Raw data are \
checksummed and set read-only; processed tables carry provenance.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"80aa757b-7122-4208-92ab-a8fb28403b6c"],

Cell["\<\
raw = RetrieveRawData[Directory[]];
processed = WriteProcessedData[Directory[], raw];
samples = processed[\"CalledSamples\"];
Length[samples]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"13b02736-270e-486f-8843-bc29c3e07abc"],

Cell["\<\
GeoListPlot[
 GeoPosition[{#[\"Latitude\"], #[\"Longitude\"]} & /@ samples],
 GeoRange -> {{34, 63}, {-12, 36}},
 PlotStyle -> Directive[Opacity[0.5], PointSize[0.004]],
 GeoBackground -> \"CountryBorders\", ImageSize -> 560]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"345eb0b9-5d13-49dc-85b6-f3fb822c2a45"],

Cell["Regional logistic reproduction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d4c76f3a-192a-44ae-b538-4f95b1c71e45"],

Cell["\<\
For each of the four analysis regions the binomial log-likelihood of a \
logistic trajectory logit p(t) = alpha + beta (10000 - t)/1000 is maximized \
directly over called alleles. Standard errors come from the numerical \
Hessian, and fits landing on a parameter bound are flagged. Binned points in \
the figure carry 95% Wilson intervals and are sized by allele count.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2fbfcf35-39c3-4ba5-b740-28167a0920c8"],

Cell["\<\
fits = FitAllRegionalLogistics[samples];
Dataset[fits]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3083035f-08be-4698-b224-2344b781da20"],

Cell["\<\
regionalOutputs = ExportRegionalFitOutputs[Directory[], samples, fits];
Import[regionalOutputs[\"RegionalFigure\"]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"bd2919b9-bc70-45a8-ab9e-f7d8c4f5cd77"],

Cell["Spatial model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3cefb369-44a4-474a-9a5a-918ae8d8069e"],

Cell["\<\
Europe is a 4-degree grid of 84 cells. Local frequency evolves in 250-year \
steps under selection s0 + sDairy D(t) m(region), modulated by a smooth \
regional dairying-onset covariate D(t), plus adjacency-based movement. One \
forward simulation costs about 26 ms, which is what makes simulation-based \
inference affordable.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"841bfca7-2ef7-4a37-b8bf-4bfa48336df0"],

Cell["\<\
grid = BuildEuropeGrid[];
Length[grid]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"3468e590-c46e-4790-a4f0-07f12e984a9d"],

Cell["\<\
AbsoluteTiming[
 SimulateSpatialTrajectory[
  <|\"InitialFrequency\" -> 0.003, \"SelectionBase\" -> 0.002,
    \"SelectionDairying\" -> 0.02, \"Migration\" -> 0.003|>, grid];]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"dfb69b10-7937-4eed-a6b5-fe31e09503a2"],

Cell["SMC-ABC inference", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"20ef946c-1e11-4107-abdd-c0d70d731d36"],

Cell["\<\
Sequential Monte Carlo ABC with an adaptive tolerance schedule (median of the \
previous population), Gaussian perturbation kernels in logit-transformed \
parameter space (so every proposal stays inside the uniform prior box and the \
prior density stays closed-form), and importance weights with ESS tracking. \
Summaries are the called-allele-weighted regional time-binned frequencies \
plus matched north-south and west-east spatial contrasts over the last 4000 \
years, so migration is informed by spatial structure. This cell takes a few \
minutes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68ccb949-01a2-4486-89da-2b046a17898f"],

Cell["\<\
smc = RunSMCABC[samples, grid, \"Particles\" -> 200, \"Generations\" -> 4,
  \"ProgressFunction\" -> Function[{g, eps, acc, ess},
    Print[\"generation \", g, \": epsilon \", eps, \", acceptance \", acc, \
\", ESS \", ess]]];
smc[\"TotalSimulations\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"31e61c65-8a11-4e51-87bd-0575296d4465"],

Cell["\<\
draws = ResamplePosterior[smc, 100];
smcOutputs = ExportSMCOutputs[Directory[], samples, grid, smc, draws];
Dataset[PosteriorParameterQuantiles[smc]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"af234f6d-90c6-4fa8-b37f-b6b61bbba692"],

Cell["Import[smcOutputs[\"ParameterFigure\"]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"fa3ce0d9-798e-456d-8634-f7b8daecd8b6"],

Cell["\<\
Each weighted posterior histogram is overlaid on its flat prior, so the \
informed dimensions (initial frequency, dairying-modulated selection, the \
northern multipliers) are visible at a glance, and the prior-dominated ones \
are equally visible. The final ESS is reported in the diagnostics table \
rather than hidden.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"18527983-0c8b-4a09-838e-2a2528ae1fad"],

Cell["Posterior predictive checks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0d37425b-bed2-46b2-af05-f21b9e1987d6"],

Cell["Import[smcOutputs[\"PosteriorPredictiveFigure\"]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cedc2aad-3efa-445a-9082-c248fc36c079"],

Cell["Held-out validation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"560560e5-2d67-4c03-be05-472c39a55be0"],

Cell["\<\
Two holdouts, both refitting the model from scratch: each region left out in \
turn, and a time-slice cut that trains only on samples older than 2500 BP and \
predicts the most recent bins. The time-slice test under-predicts the recent \
rise (large RMSE, wide covering intervals): most of the evidence for strong \
late selection lives in the last three millennia, consistent with Burger et \
al. 2020. These cells take several minutes.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"28c9026a-0264-4040-8e21-87103bea315d"],

Cell["\<\
cv = RunSMCCrossValidation[samples, grid, \"Particles\" -> 100, \"Generations\
\" -> 3];
Dataset[cv]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"7060aa56-b2dc-4af6-9c55-722bbd0a25a0"],

Cell["\<\
timeSlice = RunTimeSliceValidation[samples, grid, \"Particles\" -> 100, \
\"Generations\" -> 3];
Dataset[{KeyDrop[timeSlice, \"PosteriorPredictive\"]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"567bedb2-918e-49fa-81b3-873b809395e8"],

Cell["Sensitivity analysis", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b58be951-9620-43e3-9f1b-30cbdcb9805f"],

Cell["\<\
The full fit rerun under five scenarios: baseline, halved selection priors, \
doubled migration prior, and dairying onsets shifted 400 years earlier or \
later. The dairying-modulated selection component stays positive throughout; \
the migration posterior tracks its prior and is reported as weakly identified.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8630c71b-34c7-41de-af1a-07ab681bfcc5"],

Cell["\<\
sensitivityRows = RunSensitivityAnalysis[samples, \"Particles\" -> 100, \
\"Generations\" -> 3];
sensOutputs = ExportSensitivityOutputs[Directory[], sensitivityRows];
Import[sensOutputs[\"SensitivityFigure\"]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5a75e346-a4a8-4833-94ad-8f359fcb4604"],

Cell["Maps and animation", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9b1bfa50-2a31-4321-8d7d-e1d747dbef55"],

Cell["\<\
Kriged posterior mean frequency and 95% interval width over the coarse grid; \
ordinary kriging is a display interpolation only, the grid remains the \
inferential unit. The animation pairs both panels from 8000 BP to the present \
in 500-year steps with the ancient samples of each time window drawn on the \
map. The MP4 is encoded directly from the raster frames (H.264).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a8f3365d-cc8e-4e11-a318-bff59fcbbe28"],

Cell["\<\
spatial = ExportSpatialVisualizations[Directory[], samples, grid, draws];
Import[spatial[\"MeanMap\"]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f91ebe3e-b9c7-4703-8cc9-3eb7f609769b"],

Cell["Import[spatial[\"UncertaintyMap\"]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"aa8c79b3-7eed-4590-8204-3517061e1e01"],

Cell["\<\
ListAnimate[Import[spatial[\"Animation\"]], AnimationRate -> 1.4, \
DefaultDuration -> 12]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f3fe5628-127c-458c-afc2-1ff7b9b90637"],

Cell["Video[spatial[\"MP4\"]]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"eeed39a1-d24b-4128-9eca-b84cc7a6ad87"]
},
WindowSize->{1150, 900},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"3197ad74-86fe-4f2b-a7df-eb6a3c02b159"
]
(* End of Notebook Content *)

